WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.599 --> 00:00:04.850
Born from the minds of a New York comedy troupe
called The Tenderloins, Impractical Jokers

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:09.320
has been a reliable hit for TruTV since debuting
in December 2011.

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:13.600
Each episode consists of a series of challenges
and dares in which four friends bust each

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:17.460
other's chops by embarrassing one of their
own, usually in public, while hidden cameras

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:18.530
capture it all.

00:00:18.530 --> 00:00:23.950
The goal: good-natured humiliation, all featuring
comic improvisation in a real-world setting.

00:00:23.950 --> 00:00:27.360
"I'm gonna kill every one of yas!

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:28.660
You're all dead!"

00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:33.090
After annual cruises, world tours, and the
embarrassment-themed TBS game show The Misery

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:38.530
Index, Joe, Murr, Q, and Sal are moving from
the small screen to the big screen when Impractical

00:00:38.530 --> 00:00:41.530
Jokers: The Movie hits theaters on February
21st, 2020.

00:00:41.530 --> 00:00:44.839
But what do you need to know before heading
in?

00:00:44.839 --> 00:00:48.399
If you've watched the show, you know that
the average episode is constructed, but not

00:00:48.399 --> 00:00:49.399
scripted.

00:00:49.399 --> 00:00:53.289
The dares conceived by the Tenderloins force
them to use their improv skills in unusual

00:00:53.289 --> 00:00:58.170
situations, both to make some good TV, and
to avoid a punishment at the end of the episode.

00:00:58.170 --> 00:01:02.989
Impractical Jokers: The Movie takes the basic
concept of the series and blows it up to big-screen

00:01:02.989 --> 00:01:03.989
levels.

00:01:03.989 --> 00:01:04.989
The official synopsis?

00:01:04.989 --> 00:01:09.710
"A humiliating high school mishap from 1992
that sends the Impractical Jokers on the road

00:01:09.710 --> 00:01:13.890
in hidden camera challenges for the chance
to turn back the clock and find redemption."

00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:19.130
The movie's December 2019 trailer shows that
this early '90s element is provided by '90s

00:01:19.130 --> 00:01:24.260
superstar Paula Abdul, who meets the Jokers
and invites them to a big party in Miami…

00:01:24.260 --> 00:01:25.640
but not all of them get to go.

00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:29.750
They decide the best way to determine the
odd man out is to do what they always do:

00:01:29.750 --> 00:01:33.210
stage elaborate, competitive scenarios in
which they can embarrass each other.

00:01:33.210 --> 00:01:36.799
Whoever they collectively deem the loser of
this competition after ten events doesn't

00:01:36.799 --> 00:01:38.679
get to go to Paula Abdul's party.

00:01:38.679 --> 00:01:43.329
The trailer also gives a few sneak peaks at
some of the high-stakes humiliating situations,

00:01:43.329 --> 00:01:47.119
including one of the Jokers crawling out of
a cave, resembling Gollum from The Lord of

00:01:47.119 --> 00:01:48.119
the Rings.

00:01:48.119 --> 00:01:52.439
"I've been down there since 1987, I was looking
for the gift shop."

00:01:52.439 --> 00:01:56.119
They're also seen trying to get somebody to
help with a broken-down car with a trunk full

00:01:56.119 --> 00:02:00.090
of drugs, and engaging in what appears to
be a horseback gladiator ride.

00:02:00.090 --> 00:02:04.869
And Jokers fans will also appreciate Sal's
Jaden Smith tattoo making a cameo appearance

00:02:04.869 --> 00:02:05.869
again.

00:02:05.869 --> 00:02:09.440
All four members of the Tenderloins troupe
have co-written and co-headline the film:

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:13.500
Joseph Gatto, James Murray, Brian Quinn, and
Salvatore Vulcano.

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:17.320
You'll also spot producer and Inside Jokes
host Casey Jost.

00:02:17.320 --> 00:02:21.380
The rest of the cast is filled out by both
actors playing people the Jokers meet during

00:02:21.380 --> 00:02:25.530
their long voyage to Miami, and random strangers
who happen to get pulled into the group's

00:02:25.530 --> 00:02:26.530
staged pranks.

00:02:26.530 --> 00:02:31.430
At a 2018 San Diego Comic-Con event, Brian
Quinn stated that the movie consists of "80

00:02:31.430 --> 00:02:34.140
percent hidden camera and 20 percent storyline."

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:38.090
However, some "name" actors do show up for
cameo appearances.

00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:42.680
Expect to see Impractical Jokers : After Party
host and former NSYNC member Joey Fatone play

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:43.870
a street busker.

00:02:43.870 --> 00:02:48.550
And Kane Hodder, the man in the Jason Voorhees
hockey mask in multiple Friday the 13th movies,

00:02:48.550 --> 00:02:50.630
puts in an appearance as an imposing bodyguard.

00:02:50.630 --> 00:02:55.430
If you want to catch up before the movie debuts
in February, the show's latest slate of episodes

00:02:55.430 --> 00:02:58.960
debuts on TruTV on Thursday January 30th.

00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:04.090
This ninth season will feature the 200th episode
of Impractical Jokers on February 13th, which

00:03:04.090 --> 00:03:05.620
will be set in Los Angeles.

00:03:05.620 --> 00:03:10.430
About a week later, Impractical Jokers: The
Movie will begin rolling out to theaters nationwide.

00:03:10.430 --> 00:03:13.900
Unfortunately for those who want to know if
they should bring their kids, the MPAA has

00:03:13.900 --> 00:03:15.460
yet to announce the film's rating.

00:03:15.460 --> 00:03:19.760
That being said, there's no reason to expect
the Jokers' feature-length adventures to venture

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:22.210
too far beyond the bounds of all-ages entertainment.

00:03:22.210 --> 00:03:26.980
We'll have to wait to find out for sure, but
the show's antics are in the PG-13 realm,

00:03:26.980 --> 00:03:29.590
and fans should expect the same from the film.

